. *In order to identify spending amounts relating to the Inflation Reduction Act (IRA) we use CFDA codes. A Catalog of Federal Domestic Assistance (CFDA) number is a five digit code t
> hat uniquely identifies the grant proram for which the funding was awarded in the usaspending.gov dataset. The government grants website sam.gov stores major information for all gov
> ernment grants including a general description and the laws which authorize them. We use both the description and the associated legislation to determine which grant programs were a
> ffected by the IRA. Some grants were created and authorized by the IRA. Others already existed, but recieved additional funding from the IRA. Certain grants do not list the Inflatio
> n Recuction Act (Public Law No: 117-169) as the authorizing piece of legislation, yet they are still related. For those, the IRA changed portions of other existing public law to all
> ow or create new grants under the umbrella of pre-existing law. Thus, such laws do not list the IRA as the authorizing legislation, but they do mention the IRA in their grant descri
> ption. 
. 
